H2.1 and H2.2 are confirmed. Participants have a better comprehension of the information provided by the AR-HUD than with the C-HUD (H2.1), and they find the AR-HUD more useful (H2.2). However, the AR-HUD is viewed as less easy to understand than the bottom HUD information (the turn-by-turn icon, turn-by-turn distance, and road sign). H2.3 and H2.4 are not confirmed, as there was no effect of the HMI on both the confidence and the comfort scores.
